From dfa17d70bdb61fbbb3227da6bca9eb0a623ef205 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jurulz <60669313+jurulz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 14:20:23 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] AMMediaboard: Emulate the LAN link between Triforce
 cabinets over UDP

F-Zero AX keeps one 0x5A0-byte link block per cabinet in the media board memory and expects the firmware to mirror every cabinet's block to the others. Open a UDP socket on the port the game configures (58505 for F-Zero AX), send our own block to the other units on every SearchDevices command and copy the blocks received from the other units into the link memory. Addresses go through the existing IP address redirection table (Dolphin.ini [Core] TriforceIPRedirections), so real addresses can be mapped to the 192.168.11.x ones the game uses.
---
